TI  - Accessory cardiac bronchus.
PG  - 821-2
LID - 10.1007/s00408-014-9617-2 [doi]
AB  - Accessory cardiac bronchus is a poorly recognized, usually asymptomatic, 
      congenital abnormality of the bronchial tree. Recognition of bronchial anomalies 
      is important since they are associated with clinical complications including 
      recurrent episodes of infection, hemoptysis, and in some cases malignancy.
