DP  - 2014 Oct 15
TI  - [Therapy-resistant pneumonia].
PG  - 1271-4
LID - 10.1024/1661-8157/a001804 [doi]
AB  - We report the case of a 72 year old patient with B-symptoms and a persistent 
      pulmonary infiltrate despite an antibiotic therapy. Buds of granulation tissue 
      were found by transbronchial biopsy proving an organizing pneumonia. B-Symptoms 
      and pulmonary infiltrate were improved immediately by a therapy with steroids. 
      Even though there were reasons for a secondary organizing pneumonia due to a 
      known chronic lymphocytic leukemia and a pneumonia treated four months before, we 
      consider a cryptogenic organizing pneumonia as most probable.
