TI  - Bilorrhea secondary to bronchobiliary fistula.
PG  - 438-41
LID - 10.9738/INTSURG-D-13-00095.1 [doi]
AB  - Bronchobiliary fistula (BBF) is a rare condition which occurs most commonly as a 
      complication of hydatid cyst liver disease. The following report describes a 
      patient who presented with biliptysis 6 months following decortication of an 
      empyema that had occurred following partial hepatectomy of a colon cancer 
      metastasis. This is the only case to our knowledge that describes the 
      presentation of a BBF in this context. The patient was diagnosed with BBF and 
      successfully underwent open thoracotomy for fistulectomy and repair.
