TI  - [Diagnostic approach of interstitial lung diseases].
PG  - 957-62
AB  - The etiological diagnosis of diffuse interstitial lung disease (ILD) is based on 
      the integration of simple information gathered by interview, physical examination 
      and discriminating arguments made by some investigations of the lower respiratory 
      tract (HR-CT scan, pulmonary function tests, biological and bronchoalveolar 
      lavage results). Obtaining the diagnosis of ILD is an important step but lung 
      biopsy is rarely necessary: the key of ILD etiological diagnosis lies to obtain 
      optimal information while imposing minimal patient aggression. The diagnostic 
      approach is best when the case is subject to a multidisciplinary discussion 
      between clinician, radiologist and pathologist experienced in the field of ILD.
