DP  - 2014
TI  - Pulmonary cryptococcosis with endobronchial lesions and meningitis.
PG  - 2731-5
AB  - A 58-year-old man presented with right chest pain, anorexia, general malaise, and 
      fever. Chest computed tomography showed a mass lesion with right middle lobe 
      atelectasis. The bronchoscopy showed polypoid lesions with a smooth surface in 
      each right middle lobe bronchial lumen. The histopathology revealed the dense 
      accumulation of histiocyte-like cells with foamy cytoplasm under the bronchial 
      epithelium along with yeast-like fungi stained positively with both Alcian blue 
      and Grocott's stains. Cryptococcus neoformans was cultured from the bronchial 
      washings. We diagnosed the patient with pulmonary cryptococcosis with 
      endobronchial lesions. The fluconazole treatment was changed to liposomal 
      amphotericin-B and flucytosine after the diagnosis of cryptococcal meningitis. 
      The minimum inhibitory concentration of the fungi suggested resistance to 
      fluconazole and flucytosine. The lesion regressed after these treatments.
