TI  - Amyopathic dermatomyositis complicated with eosinophilic pneumonia.
PG  - 1539-44
AB  - A 67-year-old woman was admitted to our hospital due to dyspnea on exertion with 
      lung abnormal shadows. A transbronchial lung biopsy specimen demonstrated 
      eosinophilic pneumonia (EP). The patient also exhibited heliotrope eyelids 
      without muscle weakness, which led to a diagnosis of amyopathic dermatomyositis 
      (ADM). As we were unable to find any other causes of EP, we diagnosed her as 
      having EP associated with ADM. Dermatomyositis (DM) has been reported to be 
      associated with various interstitial lung diseases; however, only one case of EP 
      associated with DM has been reported. We herein report the first case of EP 
      complicated with ADM.
