TI  - Synchronous triple primary lung cancers: a case report.
PG  - 646-50
LID - 10.3348/kjr.2014.15.5.646 [doi]
AB  - Synchronous primary lung cancers are relatively rare. The accurate diagnosis 
      remains challenging, despite of the routine use of bronchoscopy and computed 
      tomography (CT) of the chest. Herein we report a case of synchronous triple 
      primary cancers of the right lung in a 72-year-old male patient in whom each 
      tumor presented distinct CT imaging findings.
