TI  - [Alveolar hemorrhage und cocaine: cause or coincidence?].
PG  - 1331-4
LID - 10.1024/1661-8157/a001833 [doi]
AB  - We report the case of a previously healthy young man who presented to the 
      hospital with hemoptysis and dyspnea. Hemoptysis is a frequently encountered 
      symptom in daily routine and investigations can easily be deferred to a longer 
      time frame. Our case illustrates the importance of a prompt investigation and 
      treatment of underlying causes. Furthermore one should not hesitate to include 
      rare, yet life threatening conditions in differential diagnosis.
