TI  - [Transesophageal tracheal intubation in patient with tracheoesophageal fistula 
      and double level cicatricial tracheal stenosis].
PG  - 74-7
AB  - The article deals with a case of successful anaesthesia management during the 
      surgery due to tracheoesophageal fistula and double level cicatricial tracheal 
      stenosis. Such surgeries are accompanied with technical and organizational 
      difficulties both for an anaesthesiologists and endoscopist. The article 
      discusses tactics of anaesthesia management during transesophageal balloon 
      dilatation of tracheal stenosis, transesophageal tracheal intubation and 
      respiratory techniques during the separation of tracheoesophageal fistula and 
      tracheal resection.
