TI  - Castleman's disease presenting as a tracheal mass.
PG  - 1798-800
LID - S0003-4975(13)01883-3 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2013.07.124 [doi]
AB  - Castleman's disease (CD) is a rare lymphoproliferative disorder of uncertain 
      cause. The most common site of involvement is the mediastinum. Endotracheal CD is 
      extremely rare. We report a case of unicentric, hyaline-vascular type CD 
      presenting as an obstructive tracheal mass. The tumor was successfully managed by 
      rigid bronchoscopy with argon plasma coagulation. There was no recurrence at the 
      2-month follow-up visit.
