TI  - A persistent cough related to aspiration of a nonradiopaque bone.
LID - 10.1097/01.JAA.0000446356.36860.07 [doi]
AB  - Aspiration of a foreign body by an adult often is not diagnosed until a month or 
      more after the event, because of a lack of presenting symptoms indicative of an 
      aspiration and low reliability, sensitivity, and specificity of plain film 
      radiographs. Instead, the foreign body aspiration typically is diagnosed during 
      the evaluation of other lung-related pathology.
