TI  - Bronchial venous plexus in left ventricular dysfunction.
PG  - 142-4
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0000000000000066 [doi]
AB  - Chronic pulmonary venous hypertension causes dilatation and engorgement of 
      bronchial veins because of a close communication between bronchial and pulmonary 
      veins. We report a case of severe left ventricular systolic dysfunction with 
      chronically elevated pulmonary venous pressure leading to characteristic 
      bronchoscopic findings of engorgement of bronchial veins.
