TI  - A rare cause of haemoptysis.
PG  - 69-73
LID - 10.1179/0001551213Z.0000000007 [doi]
AB  - A 59-year-old man was admitted with haemoptysis, several months after a car 
      accident. A diagnostic work-up including laboratory testing, chest radiograph and 
      bronchoscopy could not explain the haemoptysis. A pancreatic-pulmonary fistula 
      was suspected by additional CT scan. Magnetic resonance 
      cholangiopancreaticography confirmed the diagnosis, followed by surgical 
      exploration and repair.
