TI  - Management of plastic bronchitis with nebulized tissue plasminogen activator: 
      another brick in the wall.
PG  - 18
LID - 10.1186/1824-7288-40-18 [doi]
AB  - Plastic bronchitis is a rare complication of a variety of respiratory diseases 
      and congenital heart disease surgery, particularly Fontan procedure. Bronchial 
      casts with rubber-like consistency develop acutely and may cause severe 
      life-threatening respiratory distress. The management of plastic bronchitis is 
      yet not well defined. Early intermittent, self-administered nebulization of 
      tissue plasminogen activator was found to be effective in preventing 
      deterioration of acute respiratory symptoms in a patient with primary ciliary 
      dyskinesia and recurrent cast formation. Further investigation into new 
      therapeutic strategies for this devastating disease is advocated.
