TI  - Bronchial thermoplasty.
PG  - 77-86
LID - S0030-6665(13)00151-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.otc.2013.09.007 [doi]
AB  - Bronchial thermoplasty is a relatively new therapy for the management of severe 
      asthma. It involves the direct bronchoscopic application of thermal energy to 
      airways by a catheter-directed expandable basket. The airways of the lower and 
      upper lobes are treated in 3 separate sessions spaced 3 weeks apart. The therapy 
      targets airway smooth muscle, with studies showing a decrease in airway smooth 
      muscle after bronchial thermoplasty therapy. After therapy, an improvement in 
      quality of life and decrease in asthma exacerbations can be expected. Adverse 
      events can occur with bronchial thermoplasty and careful patient selection is 
      critical to ensure benefits outweigh the potential risks.
