TI  - Main bronchial stenosis--sequel of delayed diagnosis after posttraumatic 
      bronchial injury.
PG  - 146-7
AB  - Bronchial ruptures due to blunt chest traumas are rarely encountered injuries and 
      frequently late diagnosed. Once the diagnostic is established by bronchoscopy 
      surgical treatment is mandatory and usually, the results are very good. In order 
      to conserve as much as possible lung parenchyma minimal possible resection is 
      required. We present four cases managed in our department by means of main 
      bronchial sleeve resection--two on the right side and two on the left side--with 
      good outcome. We were able to save the entire lung in all four cases despite 
      long-term atelectasis.
