VI  - 59
IP  - 3
DP  - 2013 Jul-Sep
TI  - Primary tracheobronchial amyloidosis: coronal CT scan may provide clues for early 
      diagnosis.
PG  - 223-5
LID - 10.4103/0022-3859.118045 [doi]
AB  - Primary tracheobronchial amyloidosis (PTBA) is a localized form of amyloidosis. 
      The clinical signs of this condition are non-specific and diagnosis before 
      bronchoscopic examination with multiple biopsies is uncommon. We present three 
      cases of PTBA and compare findings between the thoracic imaging and fiberoptic 
      bronchoscopy. Radiographic findings often had uncharacteristic features. The 
      relatively specific coronal section CT preceded findings in transverse sections, 
      and showed an irregular mucosal surface with diffuse prominent nodes and/or 
      calcification of the tracheobronchus, which we called the "wavy path sign". In 
      conclusion, coronal CT scan can provide ample clues for the early diagnosis of 
      PTBA.
