TI  - Pulmonary artery sarcoma diagnosed by endobronchial ultrasound-guided 
      transbronchial needle aspiration.
PG  - e33-5
LID - S0003-4975(13)00387-1 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2013.01.080 [doi]
AB  - Pulmonary artery sarcoma (PAS) is a rare tumor that is often detected at an 
      advanced stage, when disease is so widespread that a radical surgical procedure 
      is no longer indicated. Therefore, less invasive biopsy techniques are required 
      to establish a definitive preoperative diagnosis. Endobronchial ultrasound (EBUS) 
      is useful for producing real-time images of both lymph nodes and the interior of 
      pulmonary arteries adjacent to the bronchi. We report a case with masslike 
      lesions in the pulmonary artery that were observed by EBUS and from which tissue 
      was obtained by endobronchial ultrasound-guided transbronchial needle aspiration 
      (EBUS-TBNA) to establish a diagnosis of PAS.
