VI  - 20
IP  - 3
DP  - 2013 Jul
TI  - Endobronchial hamartoma.
PG  - 247-8
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e31829aad50 [doi]
AB  - We present images of an endobronchial hamartoma visible by bronchoscopy in the 
      left lower lobe. A 56-year-old woman with a late presentation of an acute 
      anterior myocardial infarction requires urgent heart transplantation and 
      subsequently has trouble weaning off the ventilator. Bronchoscopic evaluation 
      reveals a 1 cm endobronchial hamartoma obstruction the left lower lobe bronchus. 
      A polypectomy snare was effectively used with electrocautery to excise the 
      lesion. The patient was successfully able to wean off the ventilator once the 
      left lower lobe was free from obstruction.
