AB  - Solitary fibrous tumours most commonly present in the pleura, but have been 
      reported in other extrapleural sites. We present a case of an elderly female who 
      was found to have a malignant solitary fibrous tumour of the right upper lobe 
      bronchus, treated with thoracoscopic lobectomy and bronchoplastic closure.
