TI  - Endobronchial biopsy of an intrapulmonary arterial mass.
PG  - 93-5
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e3182814b02 [doi]
AB  - We report a case of endobronchial ultrasound (EBUS)-guided biopsy of an 
      intrapulmonary arterial lung mass. The patient was referred to our center after 
      unsuccessful attempts to get the diagnosis using bronchoscopic-guided (including 
      EBUS) and computed tomography-guided approaches at the referring institution. We 
      attempted to cannulate the upper lobe bronchus with the EBUS scope, but the sharp 
      angle and narrow orifice would not permit the scope to view the mass or 
      surrounding anatomy. We proceeded with biopsy of the mass by traversing the left 
      main pulmonary arterial free wall and obtained diagnostic tissue without 
      complications. The patient was discharged from the procedure unit and followed up 
      with her referring physician.
