AB  - The management of a neonate with a known difficult airway is a challenge to any 
      clinician. We report a four-day-old neonate with a known difficult airway, who 
      presented to us for rigid bronchoscopy. We used an innovative, economical and 
      easily available adult central venous line guidewire to secure the airway and 
      reintubate the child.
