TI  - IgG myeloma presenting as a large mediastinal mass and pleural effusion.
PG  - 65-7
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e31823fcc5b [doi]
AB  - Plasmacytoma, a rare form of plasma cell dyscrasia, refers to a neoplastic 
      proliferation of plasma cells. Although the upper aerodigestive tract is the most 
      common site for extramedullary plasmacytoma, mediastinal and pleural involvement 
      is extremely rare. We report the case of a patient who presented with a large 
      mediastinal mass and pleural effusion. Diagnosis was challenging and subsequently 
      made as mediastinal extramedullary plasmacytoma with simultaneous myelomatous 
      pleural effusion. Further investigations revealed multiple myeloma.
