TI  - Endobronchial ultrasound-guided transbronchial needle aspiration.
PG  - 61-71
AB  - Endobronchial ultrasound-guided transbronchial needle aspiration (EBUS-TBNA) is 
      an increasingly used technique by the interventional pulmonologist in lung cancer 
      staging and diagnosis of both malignant and benign mediastinal lymphadenopathy 
      amongst other applications. There are increasing data to support the use of 
      EBUS-TBNA over mediastinoscopy as a first staging or diagnostic procedure in 
      defined situations. In this review, the technique of EBUS-TBNA is briefly 
      discussed with a more extended discussion around comparative studies of 
      mediastinal staging techniques, with an emphasis on the recent ASTER trial as 
      well as impending trials and diagnostic performance studies of EBUS-TBNA in 
      sarcoidosis.
