PG  - 111-3
LID - 10.1136/thoraxjnl-2012-201973 [doi]
AB  - We present a case of a 32-year-old woman who was diagnosed with 
      lymphangioleiomyomatosis (LAM) after detecting a mass in the upper anterior 
      mediastinum. Two years after presentation another metastatic localisation of LAM 
      occurred in the cervical region. With this article we would like to highlight the 
      fact that there are still a lot of unanswered questions, especially regarding the 
      best management of extrapulmonary LAM.
