TI  - Removal of a bullet in the pericardial cavity by video-assisted thoracoscopic 
      surgery.
PG  - 297-8
LID - 10.1093/icvts/ivs079 [doi]
AB  - The use of video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery (VATS) in dealing with thoracic 
      trauma has been well established. VATS avoids a thoracotomy and offers excellent 
      visualization of the entire pleural cavity. The removal of bullets from the 
      pleural cavity using VATS has also been reported, but, to our knowledge, this is 
      the first time a bullet has been removed from the pericardial cavity using VATS.
