TI  - Successful removal of expandable metallic stent in a patient with lung cancer.
PG  - 202-4
LID - 10.1177/0218492311431347 [doi]
AB  - A 64-year-old man, who had received chemoradiation therapy for stage IIIB 
      non-small-cell lung cancer, underwent stent insertion with a covered expandable 
      metallic stent for post-radiation bronchial stenosis. Stenosis due to formation 
      of granulation tissue at the distal stent site resulted in critical respiratory 
      failure. The stent was removed after 43 months, using rigid bronchoscopy.
