TI  - Iatrogenic tracheal rupture: bovine pericardial patch repair without flap 
      reinforcement.
PG  - 502-3
LID - 10.1093/icvts/ivr132 [doi]
AB  - We describe a case of an extensive post-intubation membranous tracheal rupture in 
      a 67-year old patient after emergency intubation. This was managed surgically by 
      bovine pericardial patch repair. Other cases of autologous and bovine patch 
      repair of tracheal lacerations exist in the literature, and we believe this is 
      the first report of successful bovine patch repair without accessory autologous 
      tissue reinforcement. This technique may be used in surgically managed cases of 
      membranous tracheal rupture where primary repair is unsuitable, thereby reducing 
      procedural complexity.
