TI  - Suspension laryngoscopy for the thoracic surgeon: when and how to use it.
PG  - 238-41
LID - S1806-37132011000200015 [pii]
AB  - Suspension laryngoscopy is one of the most common otolaryngological procedures 
      for the diagnosis and surgical approach to the larynx. However, most thoracic 
      surgeons are not familiar with the procedure and seldom use it. The indications 
      for its use are similar to those for that of rigid bronchoscopy (dilatation, 
      endoprosthesis insertion, and tumor resection). It can be performed in children 
      and adults. Suspension laryngoscopy is an alternative when rigid bronchoscopy is 
      unavailable and is therefore a viable option for use at smaller facilities. In 
      this communication, we describe the technique and the applications of suspension 
      laryngoscopy in thoracic surgery.
