TI  - [Persistent pleuropneumopathy in a young woman].
PG  - 355-8
LID - 10.1016/j.pneumo.2009.10.005 [doi]
AB  - Bronchopulmonary sequestration is a rare malformation characterized by lung 
      tissue fed by one or several aberrant systemic arteries. The authors present the 
      case of a 35-year-old woman in whom extralobar sequestration was fortuitously 
      detected at the time of persistent pleuropneumopathy. Computed tomography was 
      used in the diagnosis of pulmonary sequestration. The most common and recommended 
      treatment is the surgical removal of the pulmonary sequestration.
