TI  - Sleeve resection for delayed presentation of traumatic bronchial transection.
PG  - 54-5
AB  - Tracheobronchial disruption is uncommon in blunt chest trauma. Many of these 
      patients die before reaching the hospital. In the majority of survivors diagnosis 
      is occasionally delayed resulting in complications like airway stenosis and lung 
      collapse. Thus it is important to have radiological follow up after severe 
      thoracic trauma. Sleeve resection can be an excellent option to conserve lung 
      tissue in delayed presentation of bronchial transection.
