TI  - [Applications of noninvasive mechanical ventilation in anesthesiology and 
      postanesthesia recovery care].
PG  - 16-27
AB  - Noninvasive ventilation (NIV) can be useful to anesthesiologists working in 
      critical care units, postanesthesia recovery units, operating theaters, or other 
      settings. NIV can help in situations of acute respiratory failure or serve as a 
      preventive measure in patients undergoing interventions under local-regional 
      anesthesia or diagnostic or therapeutic procedures requiring sedation. Successful 
      NIV depends on adequately trained health personnel and the proper choice of 
      material (interfaces, respirators, etc.) for each setting where this modality is 
      used.
