TI  - Membranous obstructive Candida tracheitis as a complication of endotracheal 
      intubation and tracheostomy.
PG  - 287-9
LID - 10.1007/s00540-009-0854-0 [doi]
AB  - This report describes a rare case of acute life-threatening stridor that was due 
      to membranous obstructive Candida tracheitis, and this condition occurred after 
      long-term endotracheal intubation and tracheostomy. An obstructive membrane was 
      found 2 cm above the carina by bronchofiberscopy. The removal of the membrane 
      resulted in the complete relief of the airway obstruction.
