TI  - Tracheal ulcer due to Epstein-Barr virus-positive diffuse large B-cell lymphoma 
      of the elderly.
PG  - 147-50
LID - S2212-5345(13)00125-1 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.resinv.2013.08.007 [doi]
AB  - A 74-year-old man was referred to our hospital because of a tracheal stenosis 
      circumscribed with soft tissue density and a left pulmonary nodule. Open biopsy 
      of a right submandibular lymph node revealed diffuse large B-cell lymphoma, and 
      the malignant cells were positive for Epstein-Barr virus gene products. 
      Bronchofiberscopy revealed a tracheal necrotizing ulcer. After chemotherapy, the 
      tracheal ulcer resolved. To our knowledge, this is the first report of a case of 
      Epstein-Barr virus-positive diffuse large B-cell lymphoma of the elderly with a 
      tracheal ulcer.
