TI  - Evaluation of a disposable sheath bronchoscope system for use in the deployed 
      field hospital.
PG  - 217-9
LID - 10.1136/jramc-2013-000125 [doi]
AB  - At present, UK field hospitals use standard flexible bronchoscopes which require 
      specialised disinfection services that are not integral to the hospital. This 
      leads to prolonged turnover of used bronchoscopes as they have to be sent away to 
      external facilities, which takes 1-3 days and is dependent on air transport to 
      other facilities. In contingency operations, off site sterilisation facilities 
      may not be available. There is a need for a bronchoscope system which can be 
      rapidly cleaned and reused. We evaluated the Vision Sciences EndoSheath 
      Bronchoscopy system, which uses a disposable outer sheath to remove the need for 
      specialised disinfection. We report our experience of using this system in a 
      deployed field hospital in Afghanistan.
