TI  - [Coccidioidomycosis with manifestation on the tongue].
PG  - 548-51
LID - 10.1007/s00292-013-1834-6 [doi]
AB  - Systemic mycoses are rare but important differential diagnoses in patients with 
      imported infections. We report the case of a 51-year-old German traveller who 
      acquired coccidioidomycosis during a holiday in Arizona, USA. The disease became 
      apparent several months later primarily as a swelling of the tongue. Subsequent 
      diagnostic investigations revealed infiltration of both lungs. The causal agent 
      Coccidioides posadasii could be cultivated from transbronchial biopsy samples.
