TI  - [Primary benign schwanomma in trachea].
PG  - 1501-2
AB  - We report a rare case of a primary schwanomma in trachea causing airway symptoms 
      in a 78-year-old male. Benign tracheal tumours are often misdiagnosed as asthma 
      or chronic lung disease and should be considered in patients who present with 
      symptoms as upper airway obstruction and haemoptysis. In this case story the 
      patient was treated with endoscopic resection of the tumour.
