TI  - The changing face of outpatient bronchoscopy in 2013.
PG  - 1214-1218
LID - S0012-3692(13)60317-7 [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.13-0066 [doi]
AB  - In 2013, the outpatient hospital payment from Medicare for a transbronchial 
      needle aspiration more than doubled. At the same time, the recently updated 
      American College of Chest Physicians guidelines for the diagnosis and management 
      of lung cancer now recommend needle techniques, such as transbronchial needle 
      aspiration, over surgical staging. The convergence of these two events will 
      accelerate the existing forces of technology and economics that have been 
      influencing both the practices of outpatient bronchoscopy and mediastinoscopy and 
      the management of patients with lung cancer over the past 20 years.
