TI  - [Manujet III manual jet ventilation used in tracheobronchial foreign bodies 
      removal in children].
PG  - 187-8, 192
AB  - OBJECTIVE: To evaluate the effect of applying Manujet III manual jet ventilation 
      to remove tracheo-bronchial foreign bodies in children. METHOD: Before 2009, 62 
      patients, using the controlled positive pressure ventilation through the side 
      holes of the rigid bronchoscopy, is signed as group P. Another group J ,from 
      January 2009 to January 2012, 48 cases, utilizing Manujet III device manual jet 
      ventilation. The satisfaction rate at placed in bronchoscopy, intraoperative 
      hypoxia. removal of foreign body situation, operative time, incidence of adverse 
      reactions were recorded and contrasted. RESULT: The difference of satisfaction 
      rate in placing endoscopy between the two groups was not statistically 
      significant (P>0.05). But in operative time, intraoperative hypoxia, incidence of 
      adverse reaction rate was statistically significant (P<0.05), J group is better 
      than the group P. CONCLUSION: In the tracheobronchial foreign bodies removal, 
      application Manujet III device to manual jet ventilation can reduce the incidence 
      of intraoperative hypoxia, easier to surgical operation.
