TI  - [Swallowing or inhaling? An instrument that disappears in the throat].
PG  - 63-6
AB  - Swallowing or inhaling a foreign object does not often happen in a dental 
      practice. If however, an instrument disappears in the throat of a patient during 
      dental treatment, an adequate response on the part of the oral healthcare 
      provider is required. On the basis of 2 cases, the consequences and procedure 
      appropriate when a foreign object disappears in the throat are discussed.
