TI  - Two cases of tracheal disease misdiagnosed as difficult-to-treat asthma.
PG  - e133-7
LID - 10.4187/respcare.02350 [doi]
AB  - Initial management of patients with difficult-to-treat asthma must begin with 
      confirmation of the diagnosis. We present 2 cases of tracheal disease 
      misdiagnosed as difficult-to-treat asthma. After systemic evaluation, 
      tracheomalacia and tracheobronchial narrowing due to diffuse calcification of the 
      cartilaginous rings were found as mimicking asthma.
