TI  - [Pulmonary medicine. Four major papers in 2010-2011].
PG  - 120-4
AB  - We have selected four papers which brought major, new contributions to pulmonary 
      medicine over the last year. These publications address following issues: The 
      effect of low-dose CT-screening on lung cancer mortality; treatment of lung 
      emphysema by bronchoscopy with endobronchial valves drainage of pleural 
      infections with combined fibrinolytic agent and desoxyribonuclease; and long-term 
      treatment of COPD with azithromycin. Each of these studies has brought novel and 
      relevant information. It is too early to say that current practice has to be 
      changed following these studies. However, they certainly open from now new 
      diagnostic and therapeutic considerations on a case by case basis.
