TI  - A strange bullet which caused chylomediastinum and chyloptysis.
PG  - 372-4
LID - 10.1055/s-0032-1311543 [doi]
AB  - Chyloptysis and chylomediastinum are uncommon complications of various kinds of 
      thoracic operations, malign and nonmalign diseases. In the English language 
      medical literature, there were no cases of both chylomediastinum and chyloptysis 
      following trauma. We discuss a case of chylomediastinum and chyloptysis after 
      penetrating trauma. The patient sustained a bullet wound that caused 
      chylomediastinum and chyloptysis without damaging major structures apart from the 
      thoracic duct in the mediastinum. Following surgical intervention, the patient 
      has remained problem-free for 5 months.
