TI  - [Extended lymphadenectomy for left NSLC--case report].
PG  - 408-11
AB  - The paper brings up a topical issue in the surgical treatment of non small lung 
      cancer, namely optimal lymphadenectomy for tracking left, considering the 
      anatomical features of specific drainage. This can be achieved by various methods 
      recently introduced in the classical arsenal left lung cancer diagnosis. It's 
      presented in detail a case of extended lymphadenectomy for lung cancer non small 
      left to right paratraheal approach without ligament arterial section. The method 
      allowed a correct staging and reporting of the case more accurate prognosis. The 
      immediate goal of the authors is to discuss on this surgical technique and for 
      long term to achieve a lot with statistical significance in order to assess the 
      value of this method.
