PG  - 1717-9
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2011.09.053 [doi]
AB  - Paraganglioma of the trachea is a rare neoplasm, with fewer than 15 cases 
      reported. A 40-year-old man presented with stridor and hemoptysis. Bronchoscopy 
      demonstrated a tumor of the posterior trachea and biopsy initially suggested 
      typical carcinoid. The patient underwent surgical resection uneventfully and made 
      a good recovery. Final pathology disclosed the tumor to be a paraganglioma based 
      on immunohistology. The pathophysiology and treatment of this tumor are 
      discussed.
