TI  - Emergency bedside extracorporeal membrane oxygenation for rescue of acute 
      tracheal obstruction.
PG  - 646-9
LID - 10.4187/respcare.01417 [doi]
AB  - A 39-year-old man experienced total obstruction of a distal tracheal plastic 
      stent by a tumor mass, preventing effective ventilation and resulting in cardiac 
      arrest. Resuscitation by emergency bedside venoarterial extracorporeal membrane 
      oxygenation (ECMO) permitted time to physically remove the obstructing tumor and 
      reestablish successful ventilation and liberation from ventilatory support. We 
      review several other reported cases of emergency ECMO to resuscitate patients 
      with acute airway obstruction.
