TI  - Direct laryngoscopy and rigid bronchoscopy.
PG  - 19-25
LID - 10.1159/000334293 [doi]
AB  - Laryngoscopy and rigid bronchoscopy represent a necessary tool in the 
      otolaryngologist's arsenal. The advancement in designing smaller and more 
      versatile laryngeal equipment and fiber-optic telescopes as well as the 
      increasingly higher resolution of still and video imagery have allowed 
      otolaryngologists to better diagnose and treat many airway lesions. This chapter 
      describes the basic equipment necessary as well step-by-step description of the 
      technique to perform rigid airway endoscopy.
