TI  - Tuberculous otitis media with endobronchial tuberculosis.
PG  - 951-4
LID - 10.1007/s10156-012-0399-2 [doi]
AB  - Although tuberculosis can affect various organs and tissues, the lung is the site 
      most commonly involved. Extrapulmonary tuberculosis (EPTB) involves relatively 
      inaccessible and variable sites and is consequently often overlooked by 
      clinicians. The ear is a notably very rare site of EPTB, and the diagnosis is 
      difficult because of the variable and confusing signs and symptoms. To our 
      knowledge, this is the first case in which tuberculous otitis media and 
      endobronchial tuberculosis coexisted.
