TI  - Leiomyoma of the trachea.
PG  - 669-70
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2011.07.022 [doi]
AB  - Primary tracheal tumors are rare. Approximately 1% of them are leiomyoma. Given 
      the rarity of these lesions, optimal management has not been defined. 
      Bronchoscopic, local surgical excision and partial tracheal resection have all 
      been described. One report of recurrence after resection has been published. The 
      incidence of recurrence following local excision is unknown. We report a case of 
      an incidental tracheal leiomyoma diagnosed and treated with a combined approach.
