TI  - Bronchopulmonary infection with Lophomonas blattarum: a case report and 
      literature review.
PG  - 944-9
AB  - Human infection with Lophomonas blattarum is extremely rare. The clinical 
      manifestations of 45 cases of bronchopulmonary L. blattarum infection occurring 
      in China, including one case diagnosed and treated at the authors' hospital, are 
      described. The most common manifestations included fever, cough with 
      expectoration, chest stuffiness or shortness of breath, bronchiectasis and 
      pulmonary abscess. A course of metronidazole treatment lasting 14-38 days was 
      effective in controlling the disease. The diagnosis of L. blattarum infection 
      should be based on one or more of bronchoscopic brush smear, bronchoscopic biopsy 
      smear and bronchoalveolar lavage.
