VI  - 75
IP  - 4
DP  - 2011 Apr
TI  - A 64-year-old woman with a left upper-lung field lobulated mass.
PG  - 223-5
AB  - Pulmonary mucinous cystic neoplasia (PMCN) is an uncommon primary lung 
      malignancy. Approximately 80 cases have been reported in the literature. We 
      describe a case and review the literature on this malignancy. Our patient was 
      asymptomatic and presented with a left upper-lung field lobulated mass. Primary 
      PMCN is a spectrum of mucinous cystic lesions that should be considered as a 
      separate lung tumor entity due to its unique morphologic features and its 
      distinct clinical behavior. Prognosis is generally better than other more common 
      lung malignancies.
