DP  - 2011 Apr
TI  - Rectal adenocarcinoma metastatic to the larynx.
PG  - E28
AB  - Malignancies metastatic to the larynx are rare, accounting for fewer than 1% of 
      all laryngeal cancers with metastatic sources; the most common of these 
      metastases are cutaneous melanomas and renal cell carcinomas. Only 13 cases of 
      colon cancer and 2 cases of rectal adenocarcinoma metastatic to the larynx have 
      been previously reported in the literature. We report a new case of rectal 
      adenocarcinoma metastatic to the larynx that resulted in subglottic stenosis in a 
      60-year-old man. We also review the literature, and we discuss the presentations 
      of and treatments for this rare entity.
