IS  - 1748-5460 (Electronic)
IS  - 0022-2151 (Linking)
VI  - 125
IP  - 7
DP  - 2011 Jul
TI  - Modified endotracheal tube: emergency alternative to paediatric tracheostomy 
      tube.
PG  - 729-31
LID - 10.1017/S0022215111000636 [doi]
AB  - BACKGROUND: In an emergency, the non-availability of a conventional paediatric 
      tracheostomy tube is a therapeutic challenge for the attending surgeon. 
      OBJECTIVE: To describe a simple alternative to a paediatric tracheostomy tube for 
      use in an emergency situation. METHOD: Case report of a 14-year-old boy who 
      developed tracheomalacia following partial cricotracheal resection for subglottic 
      stenosis. As a suitably sized tracheostomy tube (with a long narrow segment) was 
      not available, an endotracheal tube was modified and used successfully. Details 
      of the modification, and a relevant literature review, are also discussed. 
      CONCLUSION: In the paediatric age group, when an appropriately sized tracheostomy 
      tube is not available, a modified endotracheal tube is a simple temporary 
      alternative; this may be especially useful in an emergency.
