TI  - Diffuse alveolar damage.
PG  - 453-63
AB  - Diffuse alveolar damage (DAD) is a characteristic histopathologic pattern that 
      has time dependent findings: intraalveolar and interstitial oedema, and hyaline 
      membranes in the acute phase, myofibroblastic accumulation in the alveolar spaces 
      and type II alveolar cell proliferation in the proliferative phase and fibrosis 
      in the more advanced phases. The diagnosis of DAD is sometimes feasible on small 
      specimens obtained by transbronchial lung biopsy or on cytological slides. 
      Surgical lung biopsy is rarely needed.
