TI  - Multidetector computed tomography aspects of tracheal mucosal leishmaniasis 
      localization.
PG  - 59-62
LID - 10.1007/s11604-010-0493-2 [doi]
AB  - Tracheal mucosal localization of Leishmania is considered a rare and dangerous 
      event. A single case of leishmaniasis of the trachea has been described in 
      literature. Our work describes multidetector computed tomography features of 
      leishmaniasis localized in the tracheal mucosa that occurred in a 68-year-old 
      patient who lived in an endemic zone. Our patient underwent biopsy that 
      established the diagnosis of leishmaniasis.
