TI  - Retrograde fiberoptic technique to avoid tracheostomy in a patient with a 
      tracheocutaneous fistula and Treacher Collins syndrome.
PG  - 255-6
LID - 10.1097/SCS.0b013e3181f7b6d1 [doi]
AB  - Children with Treacher Collins syndrome have multiple craniofacial abnormalities 
      that can cause difficulty ventilating and intubating under general anesthesia. We 
      describe a unique technique to secure an endotracheal tube via a retrograde 
      technique using patent tracheocutaneous fistula and fiberoptic bronchoscopy. In 
      this setting, the presence of a tracheocutaneous fistula spared tracheostomy in 
      this patient.
