TI  - Successful muscle prombage for directly nonclosable extremely calcified bronchial 
      stump.
PG  - 48-51
LID - 10.1007/s11748-010-0589-8 [doi]
AB  - Severe diffuse chronic calcification can cause an unsuccessful closure of the 
      bronchial stump. An opened stump must be closed with a tissue flap without 
      fixation using the bronchial wall. We performed successful volume double-layered 
      dressing using a technique whereby we divided the latissimus dorsi muscle above 
      and below the left pulmonary artery over the open stump of a severely calcified 
      bronchus.
