TI  - Interstitial lung disease associated with the idiopathic inflammatory myopathies: 
      what progress has been made in the past 35 years?
PG  - 1464-74
LID - 10.1378/chest.10-0180 [doi]
AB  - Interstitial lung disease is commonly associated with the autoimmune inflammatory 
      myopathies dermatomyositis and polymyositis and accounts for significant 
      morbidity and mortality in these conditions. In the 35 years since the 
      association between inflammatory myopathy and interstitial lung disease was 
      initially described, there has been progress in diagnosing and treating this 
      dis-order. Nevertheless, there remains much about pathogenesis and therapeutics 
      to be learned. This review examines the changes in the understanding of this 
      complex condition, highlighting recent advances and areas deserving of further 
      study.
