TI  - [Bilateral foreign bodies in the airway. Report of one case].
PG  - 470-2
AB  - Inhaled foreign bodies can be a life-threatening emergency and requires immediate 
      intervention. We report a 40-year-old man who came to the ER complaining of chest 
      pain and cough. He had lost his dental prosthesis. Chest X-Rays showed two 
      foreign bodies, one at the intermediate bronchus and the other at the left 
      posterior basal segmental bronchus. By fibrobronchoscopy, porcelain fused to a 
      metal dental crown of six teeth was extracted from the right side, and a cast of 
      metal from the left side.
