TI  - Hypoplastic left heart syndrome associated with large omphalocele and hypoplastic 
      left bronchus.
PG  - 878-80
LID - 10.1007/s00246-010-9716-7 [doi]
AB  - We present a patient with the combination of hypoplastic left heart syndrome 
      (HLHS), large omphalocele, and hypoplastic left bronchus who underwent a modified 
      Norwood procedure and was successfully discharged home. The child required 
      tracheostomy with home ventilation and we elected to delay the primary repair of 
      the omphalocele. To our knowledge, this is the first reported case with this 
      combination of anomalies surviving till hospital discharge. Our experience 
      demonstrates the potential viability of patients with concurrent HLHS, large 
      abdominal wall defects, and airway anomalies and may additionally advocate for 
      delayed repair of large omphaloceles in patients with complex congenital heart 
      disease.
