TI  - Foreign body removal using bronchoscopy and argon plasma coagulation.
PG  - 150-2
AB  - Foreign body aspiration can be a life threatening event especially for young 
      children with smaller diameters of airway size. The foreign body can result in 
      body response and granulation tissue formation around the object which makes the 
      foreign body removal difficult. In such situations surgical intervention is 
      usually needed but with interventional pulmonology modalities we can restrict the 
      need of surgery.
