TI  - Unsuspected tracheal web inhibits endotracheal intubation: report of a case.
PG  - 132-3
LID - 10.1007/s00540-009-0844-2 [doi]
AB  - A 66-year-old woman was scheduled for resection of a recurrent brain astrocytoma. 
      During anesthesia induction, endotracheal intubation became impossible. Urgent 
      bronchoscopy under laryngeal mask ventilation visualized a subglottic web 1 cm 
      below the vocal cords. After bronchoscopic ablation with argon plasma 
      coagulation, the airway intubation was successful.
