TI  - T-tube insertion for sclerotic subglottic stenosis.
PG  - 215-8
LID - 10.1177/0218492312475228 [doi]
AB  - T-tube insertion is effective treatment for subglottic stenosis, but it is 
      generally difficult due to bending of the T-tube. In a 52-year-old woman with 
      relapsing polychondritis, a T-tube was inserted after predilatation using Hegar 
      dilators. We describe the details of our T-tube insertion methods for sclerotic 
      subglottic stenosis.
