TI  - Granulomatosis with polyangiitis (Wegener's granulomatosis) diagnosed by 
      transbronchial biopsy from stenotic portion of mainstem bronchus.
PG  - 649-52
LID - 10.3109/14397595.2013.844305 [doi]
AB  - This report concerns a case of granulomatosis with polyangiitis (GPA) (Wegener's 
      granulomatosis (WG)) with bronchus narrowing. Although nasal biopsy had been 
      performed three times, no positive histology for GPA (WG) could be obtained. 
      Flexible bronchoscopy revealed diffuse erythema, edema of the mucosa and stenosis 
      of the right mainstem bronchus. Transbronchial biopsy identified granuloma with 
      giant cells. These findings led to a diagnosis of GPA (WG). This case suggests 
      that biopsy from the bronchus is useful for diagnosis of GPA (WG).
