TI  - Recurrent tracheoesophageal fistula.
PG  - 214-8
LID - 10.1055/s-0033-1347913 [doi]
AB  - Repair of recurrent tracheoesophageal fistulas (rTEFs) remains a technically 
      challenging endeavor. Although considered the gold standard, open surgical repair 
      is associated with significant morbidity and rates of recurrence. Over the last 
      40 years, endoscopic techniques have gained popularity and been touted as a safer 
      first line treatment. This review complies the published articles related to 
      endoscopic repair of rTEFs and reports the various techniques, number of 
      interventions, and success rates. Controversy will remain as to which technique 
      is superior until prospective, multi-institutional studies are performed.
