TI  - [Electromagnetic navigated bronchoscopy can be applied for diagnosing 
      peripherally located lung cancer in patients with severely reduced lung 
      function].
PG  - 1416-9
AB  - Electromagnetic navigated (EMN) bronchoscopy is a new diagnostic method, which 
      has been used in Denmark since 2008. It is a safe method for diagnosing lung 
      cancer in patients with severely reduced lung function. The method allows 
      diagnosis of peripherally located tumours. From September 2009 to January 2012, 
      the procedure has been performed in 56 patients. In total, 67 tumour evaluations 
      have been conducted. In 15 patients a cancer diagnosis was made. In two patients, 
      pneumothorax occurred. The risk of pneumothorax as a consequence of the EMN 
      procedure was 3%. This is in line with results and experiences from other 
      studies.
