TI  - Evaluation of the diagnostic utility of fiberoptic bronchoscopy for 
      smear-negative pulmonary tuberculosis in routine clinical practice.
PG  - 757-60
LID - S1806-37132012000600011 [pii]
AB  - We evaluated the diagnostic yield of fiberoptic bronchoscopy for the diagnosis of 
      smear-negative pulmonary tuberculosis in patients treated at a referral hospital 
      in Lima, Peru. Of the 611 patients who underwent the procedure, 140 (23%) were 
      diagnosed with tuberculosis based on the analysis of BAL samples. Being young and 
      being male were significantly associated with positive cultures. In addition, 287 
      patients underwent post-bronchoscopic sputum smear testing for AFB, the results 
      of which increased the diagnostic yield by 22% over that obtained through the 
      analysis of BAL samples alone. We conclude that the analysis of BAL samples and 
      post-bronchoscopic sputum samples provides a high diagnostic yield in 
      smear-negative patients suspected of having pulmonary tuberculosis.
