TI  - Small-cell cancer presenting as a tracheal polyp: a case report and review of the 
      literature.
PG  - 132-6
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e31824dd182 [doi]
AB  - Primary tracheal tumors are rare. Malignant tracheal polyps constitute the 
      majority, with very few case reports of small-cell cancer in the literature. 
      Staging of these tumors follows the lung cancer TNM staging system, with little 
      evidence-based guidance for their management. We report a case of small-cell 
      cancer presenting as a tracheal polyp and review the related literature.
