TI  - Endobronchial schwannoma.
PG  - 75-7
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e318241e5aa [doi]
AB  - Schwannomas are benign nerve-sheath tumors that arise from Schwann cells. They 
      can present as endobronchial lesions with symptoms of obstruction and hemoptysis. 
      We describe the first case of multiple endobronchial schwannomas at 3 different 
      sites in a single patient. The autofluorescence ratio was <0.5 for 2 of 3 
      lesions. The optimal follow-up and treatment plan for these lesions remain 
      unknown, especially in asymptomatic patients.
