STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20130416
LR  - 20190918
IS  - 1540-1413 (Electronic)
IS  - 1540-1405 (Linking)
VI  - 10 Suppl 2
DP  - 2012 Oct 1
TI  - Our experience with photodynamic diagnosis and photodynamic therapy for lung 
      cancer.
PG  - S3-8
AB  - The diagnosis of lung cancer was significantly enhanced by the development of the 
      fiberoptic bronchoscope in 1965. Since then, advances in photosensitizers and 
      light sources have brought photodynamic medicine into the light. This article 
      offers an historic overview of the emergence of photodynamic medicine through the 
      perspective of a pioneer with more than 30 years' experience. Along with a 
      discussion of photodynamic diagnosis of lung cancers via optical coherence 
      tomography, the curative, palliative, and neoadjuvant roles of photodynamic 
      therapy for early and advanced lung cancers are explored. An emerging strategy of 
      using PDM to treat peripheral early-stage lung tumors is briefly discussed.
