TI  - Current management of infantile hemangiomas and their common associated 
      conditions.
PG  - 545-56, vii
LID - 10.1016/j.otc.2012.03.001 [doi]
AB  - This article reviews the most current practice guidelines in the diagnosis and 
      treatment of infantile hemangiomas. Several systemic conditions that can be 
      associated with hemangiomas, such as PHACES syndrome, are also discussed. 
      Propranolol has become an effective first-line treatment, and protocols for its 
      use as well as its potential risks are outlined.
