TI  - Approach to the diagnosis of interstitial lung disease.
PG  - 1-10
LID - 10.1016/j.ccm.2011.12.002 [doi]
AB  - Interstitial lung diseases (ILDs) encompass a wide range of diffuse pulmonary 
      disorders, characterized by a variable degree of inflammatory and fibrotic 
      changes of the alveolar wall and eventually the distal bronchiolar airspaces. 
      ILDs may occur in isolation or in association with systemic diseases. The 
      clinical evaluation of a patient with ILD includes a thorough medical history and 
      detailed physical examination; obligatory diagnostic testing includes laboratory 
      testing, chest radiography, and high-resolution computed tomography and 
      comprehensive pulmonary function testing and blood gas analysis. To optimize the 
      diagnostic yield, a dynamic interaction between the pulmonologist, radiologist, 
      and pathologist is mandatory.
