TI  - [A leak in the lung: endobronchial one-way valve placement as treatment for a 
      persistent bronchopleural fistula].
PG  - 188-91
LID - 10.1055/s-0031-1291615 [doi]
AB  - Patients with bronchopleural fistula are at an increased risk of morbidity and 
      mortality. Treatment of the air leak includes intrathoracic drainage, antibiotic 
      therapy and closure of the fistula, which conventionally has been performed via 
      surgical means. In patients with limited respiratory capacity, less-invasive 
      alternatives are required. Here we report on a 62-year-old patient with 
      underlying severe COPD, who was admitted with a lung abscess and consecutively 
      developed a persistent bronchopleural fistula. Treatment involved antibiotic 
      therapy and endobronchial one-way valve placement, which resulted in termination 
      of the air leak and full recovery.
