TI  - Traumatic bronchial rupture and platypnea-orthodeoxia.
PG  - 662-4
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2011.07.072 [doi]
AB  - A patient with blunt trauma and traumatic bronchial rupture and lung collapse had 
      prominent symptoms of platypnea-orthodeoxia syndrome. These symptoms were 
      relieved by bronchial repair. The syndrome is rarely seen and is usually 
      associated with a patent foramen ovale or atrial septal defect. The syndrome has 
      not been described previously in association with traumatic bronchial rupture.
