TI  - Muscle plombage for extensive bronchial necrosis after right lower lobectomy.
PG  - 60-2
LID - 10.1007/s11748-010-0764-y [doi]
AB  - Bronchial stump necrosis is a lethal complication after pulmonary resection. We 
      report a patient who had extensive necrosis of the intermediate bronchus after 
      right lower lobectomy. The large bronchial defect was successfully fixed with 
      latissimus dorsi muscle and replaced by bronchial epithelialization.
