TI  - Amyloidosis and respiratory tract involvement: report of two cases.
PG  - 1150-3
AB  - Amyloidosis is a group of diseases in which amyloid deposit in the extracellular 
      space in an abnormal insoluble fibrillar form. The most important amyloid 
      precursors are immunoglobulin light chain (AL) and serum amyloid-associated 
      protein (AA). Amyloidosis can manifest as localized or systemic disease and 
      respiratory system is one of the target organs that can be involved by amyloid. 
      The authors report two cases of pulmonary amyloidosis presented with diffuse 
      interstitial pulmonary amyloidosis and tracheobronchial involvement.
