TI  - [Congenital bronchial atresia in adults].
PG  - 672-6
LID - 10.1016/j.rmr.2010.12.005 [doi]
AB  - Congenital bronchial atresia is a rare congenital obliteration of a segmental or 
      lobar bronchus resulting in distension of the corresponding parenchyma. It is 
      seldom diagnosed in the adult. It may lead to infectious complications and, in 
      the long term, to damage to the adjacent lung parenchyma. A surgical resection is 
      necessary and it can be achieved by thoracoscopy. We report a recent series of 
      six patients.
