TI  - Paramediastinal air cyst with traumatic bronchial injury: a rare complication of 
      neonatal resuscitation.
PG  - 236-8
LID - 10.1055/s-0030-1270946 [doi]
AB  - Paramediastinal air cysts and pneumatoceles are known complications of chest 
      trauma and mechanical ventilation. After an initial period of enlargement, these 
      lesions tend to resolve completely with conservative management. We present a 
      case of a premature newborn who developed an enlarging paramediastinal air cyst 
      as a result of resuscitation around the time of delivery that ultimately required 
      surgical excision via a right thoracotomy. To our knowledge, this is the first 
      reported case in a neonate.
