TI  - Infected mediastinal bronchogenic cyst in a 12 year old girl.
PG  - 239-41
LID - 10.1055/s-0030-1250575 [doi]
AB  - Bronchogenic cysts are an uncommon congenital malformation deriving from the 
      primitive foregut. They are mainly unilocular, and respiratory distress is the 
      most common presentation in pediatric patients. We describe the case of a 
      12-year-old girl with a huge infected mediastinal bronchogenic cyst which was 
      resected via an axillary muscle-sparing thoracotomy.
