TI  - Tracheopathia osteoplastica presenting with haemoptysis in a young male.
PG  - 119-21
AB  - A young man presented with infrequent haemoptysis spanning over 10 years. Chest 
      radiograph was normal. However, the computed tomography (CT) of the chest had 
      shown endotracheal wall changes. The diagnosis of tracheopathia osteoplastica was 
      suggested on fiberoptic bronchoscopy and confirmed histologically.
