TI  - A case of ciprofloxacin tablet aspiration.
PG  - 97-9
AB  - Foreign body aspirations occur among children more than adults and can cause life 
      threatening complications. Acute respiratory failure due to foreign body 
      aspiration in adults is a rare condition. We reported a 76-years-old woman who 
      admitted to the emergency room with respiratory failure. The chest X-ray showed 
      total collapse of the left lung. A ciprofloxacin tablet was observed and 
      extracted during the bronchoscopy. To the best of our knowledge this is the first 
      report of a ciprofloxacin tablet aspiration.
