TI  - A cluster of Teflon pledgets manifesting as an intrathoracic cavitary mass 
      following lung resection.
PG  - 250-2
LID - 10.1055/s-0029-1186134 [doi]
AB  - Teflon pledgets are widely used for hemostasis and the reinforcement of friable 
      tissue in surgery. However, rare but serious complications caused by the erosion 
      of Teflon pledgets have been reported. We present an unusual case of an 
      intrathoracic cavitary mass that was formed by the erosion of a cluster of Teflon 
      pledgets into the lung parenchyma eight years after a lung resection.
