TI  - Inflammatory myofibroblastic tumour of the lung in a five-year-old girl.
PG  - 805-6
LID - 10.1510/icvts.2009.219089 [doi]
AB  - The inflammatory myofibroblastic tumour of the lung is considered a rare 
      diagnosis of lung masses. We report the case of a five-year-old girl who 
      presented with recurrent pyrexia, dry cough, and shortness of breath. Chest X-ray 
      and computed tomography showed a total atelectasis of the left lower lobe and a 
      segmental atelectasis of the left upper lobe. The mass was removed in toto, 
      histopathology revealed the diagnosis of an inflammatory myofibroblastic tumour 
      of the lung. The patient is without any signs of relapse 30 months after surgery.
