TI  - Large mediastinal thoracic duct cyst.
PG  - 138-9
LID - 10.1510/icvts.2009.216861 [doi]
AB  - Thoracic duct cysts of the mediastinum are extremely rare. The etiology is 
      related to a congenital or degenerative weakness in the wall of the thoracic 
      duct. Symptoms may arise from compression of adjacent structures. Surgical 
      resection is recommended and allows a definitive histological diagnosis. 
      Postoperative chylothorax is the most frequent complication. We describe a 
      30-year-old female who presented to us with a history of dry cough and hiccups 
      within the last four months.
