TI  - Tracheobronchial amyloidosis managed with multimodality therapies.
PG  - 48-52
LID - 10.1177/1753465814524470 [doi]
AB  - Amyloidosis is a systemic disease involving abnormal extracellular deposition of 
      amyloid and autologous fibrillar protein material in β-pleated sheets. 
      Accumulation of this abnormal protein leads to organ dysfunction, although 
      respiratory tract involvement is rare. We present two cases of tracheobronchial 
      amyloidosis successfully treated with surgery and radiation.
