TI  - Benign granulomatous polyp obstructing the bronchus.
PG  - 519-21
AB  - Inflammatory endobronchial polyps are rarely encountered. We report a case of a 
      14 years old girl with a benign granulomatous polyp originating in the bronchus. 
      Computed tomography scan showed an intraluminal soft tissue opacity while 
      fiberoptic bronchoscopy revealed a large soft tissue mass completely occluding 
      the left lower lobe. Rigid bronchoscopy under general anaesthesia identified a 
      fleshy mass in the left main stem bronchus which was excised via bronchoscopy. 
      The histopathology showed benign polyp with non-specific inflammation. The 
      patient's symptoms improved subsequently and no recurrence was reported till two 
      years of follow-up.
