TI  - A 65-year-old female with an endobronchial mass lesion.
PG  - e95-8
LID - 10.4187/respcare.01952 [doi]
AB  - Glomus tumor is a rare, predominantly benign, soft tissue tumor. The lower 
      respiratory tract is an uncommon site of origin of glomus tumor, so endobronchial 
      glomus tumor is extremely rare. Such tumors are mostly benign and identified 
      incidentally on imaging. Diagnosis is confirmed by immunohistochemical staining, 
      and resection is the treatment of choice. We report a middle-age female with 
      endobronchial glomus tumor. This is 23rd case of reported pulmonary glomus tumor, 
      to the best of our knowledge.
