TI  - 'Non-resolving' pneumonia.
LID - 10.1136/bcr-2012-006861 [doi]
LID - bcr2012006861
AB  - A 47-year-old man presented with symptoms of fever and productive cough secondary 
      to a left upper lobe pneumonia. He had received more than three courses of 
      antibiotics over a 2-year period. Review of serial radiographic exams including 
      chest x-ray and CT scans revealed consolidation of the left upper lobe. Lack of 
      response to antibiotics prompted invasive testing with bronchoscopy which 
      revealed a growth in the left main bronchus. Histopathology revealed squamous 
      cell carcinoma.
