TI  - Gustav Killian: beyond his dehiscence.
PG  - 1164-8
LID - 10.1017/S0022215112001764 [doi]
AB  - For most doctors, Gustav Killian is best known for his eponymous pharyngeal 
      dehiscence. Otorhinolaryngologists may also be familiar with his contributions to 
      rhinology by way of his well-known incision and speculum. Few, however, will be 
      aware of the true significance of his contributions to medicine. Killian was at 
      the forefront of advances in ENT surgery at the turn of the twentieth century. 
      From his early years to his revolutionary work on bronchoscopy and a narrowly 
      missed Nobel Prize, this paper reviews the life and works of a most prolific and 
      often overlooked surgical innovator.
