TI  - Mediastinal lymph node staging: from noninvasive to surgical.
PG  - W54-64
LID - 10.2214/AJR.11.7446 [doi]
AB  - OBJECTIVE: The purpose of this review is to describe the current lymph node 
      stations and lymph node staging of non-small cell lung carcinoma. Minimally 
      invasive and invasive methods of mediastinal lymph node staging are emphasized, 
      and the relative accuracy and limitations of each modality are described. 
      CONCLUSION: Lung carcinoma remains the most common cause of cancer death in the 
      United States. Accurate staging of lung cancer is imperative for implementing the 
      correct therapy and assessing patient prognosis.
