DP  - 2013 Mar
TI  - Fish fin aspiration: an unusual type of lower airway foreign body in a Chinese 
      adult.
PG  - e20-2
LID - 10.4187/respcare.01971 [doi]
AB  - Foreign body aspiration into the lower airway is rare in adults, and typically 
      occurs in individuals of advanced age or with underlying neurological or medical 
      conditions. The most common type of lower airway foreign body is organic 
      substances, in particular chicken or fish bones. In many patients a history of an 
      acute choking event is not found, and symptoms are non-specific and may be 
      attributed to other medical conditions. Herein we report the unique case of an 
      80-year-old Chinese woman who aspirated a fish fin that was undiagnosed for 3 
      years.
