DP  - 2012 Jun
TI  - Development of massive pneumopericardium after intubation and positive pressure 
      ventilation.
PG  - 401-2
AB  - Pneumopericardium is a rare complication of chest trauma, mechanical ventilation 
      and cavitating pneumonia. We report a case of a 7-year-old patient with chronic 
      myeloid leukemia who developed massive pneumopericardium immediately after being 
      electively intubated for a diagnostic radiological procedure in the setting of 
      ongoing Enterococcal pneumonia. As intensive care medicine becomes more prevalent 
      in hospitals, we believe that clinicians need to be aware of this uncommon but 
      potentially fatal condition.
