TI  - Farmer's lung-induced hypersensitivity pneumonitis complicated by shock.
PG  - 464-6
LID - 10.4187/respcare.01191 [doi]
AB  - Hypersensitivity pneumonitis is an immunologic reaction to an inhaled antigen, 
      with a wide spectrum of clinical presentations. The most common manifestations 
      are fever, cough, and dyspnea. We describe a case of hypersensitivity pneumonitis 
      with marked alveolar lymphocytosis; the patient presented with respiratory 
      failure and shock requiring mechanical ventilation and vasopressive agents. We 
      hypothesized that immune mediators implicated in the pathogenesis of 
      hypersensitivity pneumonitis were responsible for the transient shock observed in 
      this patient.
