TI  - A rare case of concurrent multiple primary lung cancer of different histological 
      types.
PG  - 181-3
AB  - Occurrence of concurrent multiple primary malignancies with different 
      histopathological presentations of the same organ at the same time is often not 
      diagnosed and rarely reported in the literature. We present a case of multiple 
      primary lung cancers with hepatic metastasis where the patient had a moderately 
      differentiated adenocarcinoma of the right lower lobe and a moderately 
      differentiated squamous cell carcinoma of the right upper lobe.
