TI  - Subcutaneous emphysema and pneumomediastinum due to foreign body aspiration in 
      children with asthma.
PG  - 88-90
LID - 10.1002/ppul.21506 [doi]
AB  - Pneumomediastinum (PM) and subcutaneous emphysema (SCE) are well recognized as 
      complications of acute asthma exacerbation in children with asthma. We present 
      herein a report of three cases of asthmatic children who presented with PM and 
      SCE found to be secondary to foreign body aspiration. The cases highlight that 
      clinicians must remain vigilant for co-morbidities in an asthma exacerbation, and 
      less common etiologies of PM and SCE, such as foreign body aspiration, should 
      also be carefully considered in asthmatic children.
