TI  - Transesophageal bronchoscopic ultrasound-guided fine-needle aspiration for 
      diagnosis of peripheral lung cancer.
PG  - 1613-6
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2010.10.054 [doi]
AB  - Peripheral lung cancer is still a diagnostic challenge. The transbronchial 
      approach with bronchoscopy or the transthoracic approach with radiologic imaging 
      has been used extensively for the pathologic diagnosis of peripheral lung cancer. 
      However, the explorability or feasibility with these modalities depends on the 
      lesion location or patient's respiratory function. Herein, we report a case with 
      severe pulmonary emphysema and lung cancer located at a parenchymal region 
      difficult to access through an airway with a bronchoscope. Successful diagnosis 
      was obtained by a transesophageal ultrasound-guided needle aspiration using an 
      endobronchial ultrasound bronchoscope. This technique is accurate and less 
      invasive in the primary diagnosis of lung cancer adjoining the esophagus.
