TI  - The solitary pulmonary nodule: approach for a general surgeon.
PG  - 1003-18
LID - 10.1016/j.suc.2010.07.002 [doi]
AB  - The solitary pulmonary nodule is a common finding on radiographic studies 
      performed for other reasons. It is important that the probability of malignancy 
      be assessed when these nodules are found. This chapter outlines a diagnostic 
      approach for these nodules to optimize non-invasive and invasive testing, and 
      describes the value of the various modalities used to evaluate these 
      abnormalities.
