TI  - A new technique for T-tube insertion in patients with subglottic stenosis.
PG  - 130-1
LID - 10.1016/j.ejcts.2010.05.014 [doi]
AB  - A silicone T tube is widely used for the management of airway problems. 
      Montgomery described the way in which it is usually inserted, but this 
      conventional insertion technique can fail in cases of subglottic stenosis due to 
      the softness of the T tube, which kinks when forced against resistance. An 
      adjunct to the traditional technique of Montgomery may help to insert a T tube in 
      such patients.
