TI  - A patient with massive hemoptysis treated by videothoracoscopic clipping of the 
      causative aberrant artery.
PG  - 253-4
LID - 10.1055/s-0029-1240781 [doi]
AB  - Massive hemoptysis is a life-threatening situation and can have a variety of 
      underlying causes. Bronchial arteries are mostly the source of bleeding but in 
      rare cases an aberrant systemic artery may be present, causing hemoptysis. Here, 
      we present a patient in whom an aberrant systemic artery was defined to be the 
      cause of hemoptysis. Obstruction of this artery by videothoracoscopic clipping 
      was curative for the patient's hemoptysis.
