DP  - 2010 Jun
TI  - Peroperative fiducial placement for postoperative stereotactic Cyberknife 
      radiosurgery.
PG  - 1034-6
LID - 10.1510/icvts.2009.227348 [doi]
AB  - Radiotherapy is often the treatment used for inoperable early-stage lung cancer 
      as well as pulmonary metastases. In the last decade, efforts were done to 
      increase local control with high-dose radiation without excessive collateral 
      damage. Initially used for cranial lesions, stereotactic radiosurgery enlarged 
      extracranial indications; the Cyberknife radiosurgery system needs metal (gold) 
      markers for image guidance. For lung tumours, fiducials are inserted computed 
      tomography (CT)-guided or bronchoscopy-guided. We describe four patients where 
      fiducial placement was done during surgery.
