TI  - Navigational bronchoscopy: overview of technology and practical 
      considerations--new Current Procedural Terminology codes effective 2010.
PG  - 450-4
LID - 10.1378/chest.09-2003 [doi]
AB  - Navigational bronchoscopy provides a three-dimensional virtual "roadmap" that 
      enables a physician to maneuver through multiple branches of the bronchial tree 
      to reach targeted lesions in distal regions of the lung. It is designed to be 
      used with a standard bronchoscope to facilitate obtaining tissue samples and for 
      placing radiosurgical or dye markers. This article overviews this technology and 
      the Current Procedural Terminology codes that have been created for its use.
